# Build-context filter for deploy/compose/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to the context root's
# `.dockerignore`, so this stays scoped to the medos image instead of imposing a filter on
# every future build in the repo.
#
# The context is the REPOSITORY ROOT (docker-compose.yml sets `context: ../../..`), because
# the image installs the `medos` package and pyproject.toml lives at the top. Without this
# file the context is ~3 MB of specification plus the whole .git directory, which is
# uploaded to the daemon on every build.

# Everything, then re-admit exactly what the Dockerfile COPYs. An allow-list, because a
# deny-list silently starts shipping whatever the next directory added to the repo is.
*
!medos/medos
!pyproject.toml
!medos/deploy/compose/requirements.txt
# The Service Plane and the registry DATA of the capabilities it ships. See the Dockerfile
# block that COPYs them: `medos/services/` is not part of the `medos` distribution, and
# `medos/examples/lung-nodule/` carries that capability's applicability envelope and coded-concept
# overlay, both of which are read at run time.
!medos/services
!medos/examples/lung-nodule
# TWO files out of medos/tools/, named one at a time. The default is to exclude medos/tools/
# entirely, and admitting a directory rather than a file would let a future script
# into the serving image without anybody deciding to put it there.
#   publish_model.py -- the publish half of the packaging step.
#   demo/seed_corpus.py -- the synthetic demo study, behind `--profile demo` and
#     refusing unless MEDOS_ENV is exactly `dev`.
!medos/tools/publish_model.py
!medos/tools/demo
# The coded-concept dictionary, and ONLY that file out of the frozen spike tree.

# Re-exclusions inside the admitted tree. `**` patterns are applied after the `!` rules.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
